<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran sticks to Hormuz plan after Trump rejects it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2df6dfaa679e81adc87f56a5ec199bd46af37124929eb188bb78267ac2d5b59e</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432--8e8b9e348264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials that while they were aware of Trump's comments on rejecting the new proposal, they had not received a formal message rejecting the plan that would open the Strait of Hormuz.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>No public mentions of Taiwan at official Xi and Trump meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8aba3cdb990d686a52f19127d1094ab2dc002e2609a7234b86297e0160beb7e8</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378--29352cbff0b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a high-profile summit between Presidents Donald Trump and Xi Jinping in Washington, there was much talk of trade and artificial intelligence. One of the most contentious issues, Taiwan, was only discussed in private.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful storm batters northeast US, hundreds of flights canceled</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a64c926e72f48e2ec0effe839499617e730740b18fe396ef44e2c6857259303</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T03:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676--6ec8e25a25ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of flights were canceled and thousands were delayed as a nor'easter brought flooding, power cuts and travel disruption to cities like New York, Boston and Philadelphia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26afe7198032abae579fdc0ea6e4a60732bc50e0cb92d97b97fb5a56ad9ea720</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia expected to intensify hybrid war on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:176b48bdddc1ff3977daab792cb178f603d845e2327245da726a06b2cff76f76</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596--b27c55cf76ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone explosions, airspace violations, arson attacks: Poland, Romania, and Moldova are now regularly targeted in Russian attacks against Ukraine. More governments are calling these attacks deliberate acts of aggression.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Suicide attack at police stop kills at least 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afb297aee3573205f4e740538d37f7f20c65e6674516c7732f8bdeaf62e638fe</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050--24fa32f41a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The blast was claimed by the Pakistani Taliban, which has stepped up attacks on Pakistani security forces in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian students: Propaganda in school prepares them to die</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56c3178a254ac856131dfbb18b4557827ae1c254e71796df18e4ca5284754efe</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-students-propaganda-in-school-prepares-them-to-die/a-79417294--87c160f62f80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-students-propaganda-in-school-prepares-them-to-die/a-79417294?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian government wants children to learn about patriotism from an early age. DW spoke to students in Siberia about their views on propaganda at school on the war in Ukraine and their future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63dd9ae66e60c49dbeca22656da8ac15dabf50bd82a01ec20ea7d6a48c970577</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lula or Bolsonaro as president? Brazil gears up to vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4165f0d8cbd8bf15c0389f4e7f4e292da0be367b0271aeb4b80d663d395e382c</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276--a6f357f68a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilians go to the polls on October 4. The front-runners are multilateralist incumbent Lula da Silva and former President Jair Bolsonaro's son, Flavio, who wants to bring Brazil closer to the US and away from China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian President Pezeshkian brought a diplomatic tone to New York for UNGA. What did his remarks signal?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:000de98c486acea5b342d12625127f6f891604d5f2373dfa18352f55d1834753</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-sig/a-79428890--b543693f4fe7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-signal/a-79428890?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's president used his trip to New York this week for the UN General Assembly to signal openness to talks over the nuclear dispute. However, the chances of a major breakthrough on the war remain low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Lithuanian skies are NATO skies': DW speaks with Lithuanian premier Mindaugas Sinkevicius</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:480e0f43293acaf7994c4baf6055590bbbc1b524a13fb27442804dfba17c2ea3</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394--2e48449cf03c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lithuanian-skies-are-nato-skies-dw-speaks-with-lithuanian-premier-mindaugas-sinkevicius/a-79432394?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a DW interview, Prime Minister Mindaugas Sinkevicius discussed threats to Lithuania from Russia and Belarus, NATO's need for stronger air defense and why military spending alone cannot ensure security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
